<article><p class="section-index">SYNVOX · NODE.JS</p><h1>From download to your first chat</h1><p class="guide-lead">A free-for-personal-use ZIP archive for macOS, Windows and Linux. No activation or subscription is required. A preview for testing, not a native installer. Alpha version 0.5.65.</p>
<div class="guide-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/downloads/synvox-desktop-0.5.65.zip" download>Download SYNVOX 0.5.65 · ZIP</a><a class="button button-quiet" href="/downloads/synvox-desktop-0.5.65.zip.sha256">SHA-256</a></div>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>1. Install Node.js</h2><p>Install Node.js 22 from the official website for your operating system and processor. npm is included. Open a new terminal window and check the versions. You need internet access and your own AI provider account.</p><a href="https://nodejs.org/en/download">Node.js ↗</a><pre><code>node --version
npm --version</code></pre></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>Python for Qwen/DeepSeek sign-in</h2><p>The sign-in browser requires Python 3.10+. On Windows, enable adding Python to PATH during installation and open a new terminal. On first connection, SYNVOX downloads Camoufox and its browser; Settings → Accounts shows progress. PyPI and GitHub downloads must be reachable.</p><a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">Download Python ↗</a></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>2. Extract the archive</h2><p>Windows: right-click the ZIP → Extract All. macOS: double-click the ZIP. Linux: use Extract in your file manager. Use a separate SYNVOX folder. Do not run inside the ZIP or extract over an older version.</p></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>3. Install dependencies</h2><p>Open the folder containing package.json. Windows: enter cmd in the File Explorer address bar and press Enter. macOS/Linux: type cd followed by a space in Terminal, drag the extracted folder into the window and press Enter. Run the command and wait for dependencies and browsers to download; this may take several minutes.</p><pre><code>npm ci</code></pre></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>4. Start the application</h2><p>Run this in the same folder. Keep the terminal open. For later launches, only this command is needed. Press Ctrl+C in the terminal to stop.</p><pre><code>npm start</code></pre></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>5. Connect an AI and a project</h2><p>Select a provider and sign in to your account using the offered login window. Create a chat, select a model and project folder. First ask for an overview without file changes. Review permissions in Settings before edits and commands. Use a project copy or a separate Git branch. Third-party accounts and limits are not included.</p></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>6. Access to SYNVOX</h2><p>SYNVOX is free for personal use: no activation, payment, or renewal is required. An installation key can remain in Settings for compatibility with older versions, but it no longer controls feature access.</p></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>Troubleshooting</h2><details><summary>node or npm not found</summary><p>Install Node.js 22, close and reopen the terminal, then check the version again.</p></details><details><summary>package.json / ENOENT error</summary><p>Change to the extracted folder containing package.json and retry.</p></details><details><summary>Browser download failed / Linux libraries missing</summary><p>Check your connection and retry npm ci. Linux may require browser system libraries. Send the exact error to support; do not disable system security.</p></details><p>Need help? Send your OS, Node.js version and error text. Remove keys, cookies and passwords. <a href="mailto:stas.sor@gmail.com">stas.sor@gmail.com</a></p><a href="/en/documents/">Terms, data and refunds</a></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>Windows: step by step</h2><ol><li>Install Node.js 22 LTS using the official Windows MSI installer. Keep npm and PATH enabled.</li><li>Download the SYNVOX ZIP. In Downloads, right-click → Extract All. Open the inner SYNVOX folder containing package.json, bin and src.</li><li>Click the File Explorer address bar, type <code>cmd</code>, and press Enter. Do not run as administrator.</li><li>Run the commands below one at a time. Wait for npm ci to finish. If PowerShell blocks npm.ps1, use Command Prompt or npm.cmd ci and npm.cmd start; do not disable execution security.</li></ol><pre><code>node --version
npm --version
npm ci
npm start</code></pre></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>macOS: step by step</h2><ol><li>Install Node.js 22 LTS from the official website, then open a new Terminal window.</li><li>Double-click the ZIP in Finder. Move the extracted SYNVOX folder to Documents, for example.</li><li>Open Applications → Utilities → Terminal. Type <code>cd</code> followed by a space, drag the SYNVOX folder into Terminal and press Enter.</li><li>Run <code>ls</code> and confirm package.json is listed. Run <code>npm ci</code>, wait until it finishes, then run <code>npm start</code>. Do not use sudo.</li></ol></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>Linux: step by step</h2><ol><li>Install Node.js 22 or newer and npm using the official instructions for your distribution. Check node --version and npm --version.</li><li>Extract the ZIP. Open a terminal in the SYNVOX folder containing package.json.</li><li>Run <code>npm ci</code>, then <code>npm start</code>. A graphical desktop session is required. If browser libraries are missing, send the exact error to support; do not run as root or disable the browser sandbox.</li></ol></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>First login</h2><ol><li>Wait for SYNVOX to open; initial browser preparation may take longer. Keep Terminal open.</li><li>Select a provider and sign in on the provider's own page. Complete any CAPTCHA or login confirmation yourself. Never send account passwords in chat.</li><li>Open a project copy, create a chat, select a model and ask: “Reply with one word: ready.” Then ask it to describe the project without modifying files.</li></ol><p>Qwen multi-account management is in Settings → Accounts. Add another account and enable automatic switching. Switching applies to supported Qwen quota responses, not every error or every provider.</p></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>Restarting, stopping and updating</h2><p>For subsequent launches, open Terminal in the same SYNVOX folder and run <code>npm start</code>. You do not need npm ci every time. Stop the application with Ctrl+C in Terminal.</p><p>Before a manual update, stop the app and keep the old folder. Extract the new version into a separate folder, run npm ci, then npm start. Do not delete user data or authentication folders. Startup output should show <code>ai-free@0.5.65</code>. This ZIP is not an EXE/DMG installer and does not enable automatic updates.</p><p>If EADDRINUSE / “port already in use” appears, close your existing SYNVOX instance first. For npm network failures, check your connection and retry; do not disable certificate verification. For a blank window, send the last Terminal error lines to support after removing keys, passwords and cookies.</p></section>

<section class="guide-section"><h2>Computer control: operating system requirements</h2><p>Chat, project tasks and built-in browser snapshots are available independently of the desktop session. Select Computer in the current chat to use screen, mouse and keyboard tools.</p><ul><li><strong>Windows:</strong> requires an active user desktop; do not run SYNVOX as a service. Shell commands use <code>cmd.exe</code>. PowerShell can be invoked explicitly as an installed program.</li><li><strong>macOS:</strong> grant Screen Recording and Accessibility to the process launching SYNVOX in System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security.</li><li><strong>Linux:</strong> requires a graphical X11 session and DISPLAY. Wayland desktop control is not supported yet. Ubuntu/Debian may need <code>libxtst6 libxrandr2 libxi6</code>; install browser dependencies with <code>npx playwright install-deps chromium</code>.</li></ul><p>Native modules are npm dependencies. If @jitsi/robotjs is missing, retry npm ci and retain the installation error. Full Windows input and multiple monitors still require manual acceptance. This ZIP remains an alpha.</p></section>
<section class="guide-section"><h2>Report a problem</h2><p>Select Report error beside an error, or Settings → Status → Report a problem. Add a description and optionally an image, then select Prepare report. Review the data and save the file. Online intake is not enabled yet; reports are not sent automatically. Do not include passwords, keys or other people’s data.</p></section>
